// @test regression/lint-lookahead-bias
// @description lookahead splits the un-offset request.security into two rules. lookahead_on with no offset returns the requested period's value from the START of the period, so on historical bars it reads data that did not exist yet - LOOKAHEAD_BIAS, fixed by adding the offset and keeping lookahead_on. lookahead_off, written or defaulted, leaks nothing (history settles on the period's final value) and only repaints against realtime - REPAINTING_SECURITY, and a lower-timeframe request needs no change at all. Emitting the future-leak wording for both invited a fix that shifts every signal by one HTF bar. Neither value ever exempts a call (INV152). TV is silent on every line. See INV153.
// @expects parse: success
// @expects warnings: 4
// @expects warning: line=3, message=/did not exist yet/
// @expects warning: line=4, message=/did not exist yet/
// @expects warning: line=5, message=/repaints/
// @expects warning: line=6, message=/repaints/
//@version=6
indicator("lookahead", overlay = true)
leakNamed = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
leakPositional = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", high, barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
repaintExplicit = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
repaintDefault = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close)
okOffsetOn = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
plot(leakNamed + leakPositional + repaintExplicit + repaintDefault + okOffsetOn)
